{"name":"Admiration","hex":"#f6f3d3","fetched":"2026-10-19","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"admiration","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A positive emotion combining wonder and approbation; the regarding of another as being wonderful; a feeling of respect for another's skills or attributes, as one might look on a hero or role model.","Wondering or questioning (without any particular positive or negative attitude to the subject)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/admiration"}],"entries":[{"title":"Admiration","blocks":[{"text":"Admiration is a social emotion felt by observing people of competence, talent, virtuous actions, or skill exceeding standards. Admiration facilitates social learning in groups. Admiration motivates self-improvement through learning from role-models. Admiration is not automatically induced, but is built from active mental evaluations of social and real world knowledge."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-_Admiration_%281897%29.jpg/330px-William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-_Admiration_%281897%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Admiration","wikidata":"Q2824657"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-_Admiration_%281897%29.jpg/500px-William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-_Admiration_%281897%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-_Admiration_%281897%29.jpg/1280px-William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-_Admiration_%281897%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-_Admiration_%28189